{"kind":"request","text":"Make the UI resilient to an out-of-range durable timestamp (finding #4 of the 2026-08-11 security assessment at main 8f22ba52; re-verify at the implementation head). EventTime (ui/src/components/EventTime.tsx:9) calls new Date(timestamp*1000).toISOString(), which throws RangeError when timestamp*1000 exceeds +/-8.64e15 ms; the committer date is parsed as an unbounded int64 (internal/gitstore/gitstore.go:305) and carried into the projection with no range check (internal/workroom/fold.go). There is no React error boundary (ui/src/main.tsx mounts \u003cApp/\u003e bare), and React 19 unmounts the whole tree on an uncaught render throw, so one poisoned durable record crashes the entire UI persistently (a reload does not help). Direction: guard the Date conversion (validate/clamp the timestamp, degrade like eventTimestamp in lib/util.ts does) AND add a top-level error boundary so a single bad record degrades one row, not the app.","body":{"conditions":"EventTime renders a safe fallback for an out-of-range or invalid timestamp instead of throwing; a React error boundary prevents a single render throw from unmounting the tree; a UI test covers an out-of-range timestamp; the UI test/build gate passes; request/ branch, independent review at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 8f22ba52; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}